&lt;/div>&lt;p>It stores the token in redis. The key is in the following format:&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Get User Real Ip</title><link>https://travisbikkle.github.io/en/2024/07/get-user-real-ip/</link><pubDate>Mon, 15 Jul 2024 10:20:57 +0800</pubDate><author>zhaoyu025@gmail.com (Travis Bikkle)</author><guid>https://travisbikkle.github.io/en/2024/07/get-user-real-ip/</guid><category domain="https://travisbikkle.github.io/en/categories/back-end/">Back-End</category><description>&lt;p>It&amp;rsquo;s a pretty simple question, but in the process of information dissemination, some mistakes happen.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>For example, some people will say, just configure X-Real-Ip, and that&amp;rsquo;s it.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Or some people will ask, what is the difference between X-Real-Ip and X-Forward-For, and what is the principle?&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Obviously, they misunderstood &lt;code>X-Real-Ip&lt;/code>.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>This article will show you what X-Real-Ip is.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="quick-answer" class="heading-element">&lt;span>Quick Answer&lt;/span>
 &lt;a href="#quick-answer" class="heading-mark">
